  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-canvas-flow",
      "text": "**English** | [简体中文](./README.zh-CN.md)\n\n> **Build your workflow on an infinite canvas.**\n> Drag cards into a flow, connect them to pass data, and watch every step happen.\n\n**dsh-canvas-flow** is an **infinite canvas plugin** running on [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness): a whole project lives on one canvas — text cards write specs, design cards produce design drafts, app cards build runnable web applications, and you can refine any element right in the preview."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-canvas-flow",
      "text": "Cards reference each other through connected edges: upstream artifacts feed directly into downstream cards, and a few cards working together can carry large, complex tasks.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Generate requirement documents with text cards, website designs or presentations with design cards, web applications with app cards, and images / videos with media cards."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **The project folder is organized by card type**: artifacts no longer sit flat in the canvas root — text goes to `docs/`, apps to `apps/`, designs to `designs/`, images to `images/`, videos to `videos/`, audio to `audio/` (plus `data/`, `files/`, `folders/`).\n  Older canvases are **tidied automatically the first time you open them**: only items sitting flat in the root are moved, one item per entry, with a numeric suffix on name clashes; anything that cannot be moved stays where it is. The root `index.html` and subdirectories you have already organized are left untouched."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Every card type supports export.\n  - Text cards: export as Markdown, plain text, Word, or PDF documents.\n\n- Design cards: export as Figma files, images, PDF, or PowerPoint.\n\n- App cards: export the web application as a zip archive — double-click `index.html` to run it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installing the plugin",
      "text": "Install the plugin from the DeepSeek Harness client.\nSearch for `dsh-canvas-flow` in the plugin marketplace and click install."
    },
    {
      "section": "Shipped",
      "text": "| Capability | Status |\n|------|------|\n| **Text** | The agent writes Markdown documents; export as Markdown, plain text, Word, or PDF |\n| **Design** | The agent produces design drafts and makes precise second-pass edits to specific layers. Export as Figma files, images, PDF, or PPT |\n| **App** | The agent writes web application code that runs directly in the DeepSeek Harness client. Pick any element and the agent precisely edits that element's code |\n| **Image** | The agent generates images (Jimeng / Seedream) onto the card's artifact, with image-to-image via reference edges; keep talking in the session to keep iterating. Export the original image, or import one from your machine as the artifact |\n| **Video** | The agent generates short videos (Jimeng / Seedance) with aspect ratio, duration, and resolution controls; a per-minute async task you wait on. Export the original clip, or import one from your machine |\n| **Audio** | The agent generates audio (Doubao `doubao-seed-audio-1-0`): dialogue, sound effects, music, and ambience all go into one prompt; synchronous, up to 120 seconds per call. Export the original file |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Shipped",
      "text": "Media generation uses **the host's own model configuration**: add a provider route in DeepSeek Harness's model settings that can serve Seedream / Seedance / Seed-Audio (fill in `baseURL` and `apiKeyEnv`) — no plugin-side configuration needed.\nWhen no usable route is found, the card tells you exactly what it searched by and where to add one."
    },
    {
      "section": "Shipped",
      "text": "One thing to know about audio: `doubao-seed-audio-1-0` is listed in Ark's model marketplace, but **the API lives in Doubao Speech** — its endpoint and key are not the same set as Ark's (auth is `X-Api-Key`, not Bearer). A dedicated route is recommended:\n\n```yaml\ndoubao-audio:\n  apiKeyEnv: ARK_AUDIO_KEY        # the API Key from the speech console\n  baseURL: https://openspeech.bytedance.com/api/v3\n  models:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Shipped",
      "text": "A single Ark route can also work (the plugin re-routes audio requests to the speech host), provided that key is valid on both sides; if it is not, the 401 message tells you exactly which route to add."
    },
    {
      "section": "Shipped",
      "text": "**The card face is the artifact itself**: an image card is the image; video and audio cards carry their native players — play them here, drag the progress bar. Every card on the canvas shares one size, **400×252**, and the media card face is **exactly 16:9**: the face is the picture. In a 200-wide card a 16:9 image is a narrow strip; and if the height were doubled (280), a 16:9 image would leave a band of background above and below — so the height is derived from the panel's 16:9 (398×224 + 26 card header + 2 border). Audio cards share the same size (one rhythm across the canvas since v1.79). The card face and the double-click full-screen preview **read the same artifact and say the same things** (file not yet generated / file too large)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Shipped",
      "text": "**\"Which model powers this conversation\" and \"which model generated this card\" are two different things that one dropdown asks**: on text / design / app cards it selects the model for the session's next request (so only conversational models are listed — picking Seedream / Seedance there would only fail the next turn); on image / video / audio cards it selects **which model generates this card**, listing only that family (Seedream on image cards, Seedance on video cards), stored on the card itself and **never touching the session**. Unset, it shows \"auto\", meaning pick by model family from the DSH model configuration above. When set, it is really used — if the configuration no longer has it, the card reports an error honestly (it never silently switches to another model); the choice travels with the work, and opening the same folder on another machine keeps it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Shipped",
      "text": "**One reference image is all image-to-image / image-to-video needs**: connect an edge from an image card to another image or video card, and on generation that edge becomes the reference (the `image` input for image-to-image, the first frame for video) — no need to publish the image as a URL first. For video you can also choose whether it is the first frame (default), the last frame, or a reference image."
    },
    {
      "section": "Next up",
      "text": "| Capability | Plan |\n|------|------|\n| **Media editing desk** | Inpainting / outpainting / matting for images, first & last frame plus camera control for videos — as parameter panels on the node, not just conversation requests |\n\n---"
    },
    {
